{#
  module/Books/view/books/library-imports/index.phtml — the imports run against one
  library.

  **The empty case is the reason this page changes.** `LibraryImportsController::
  indexAction()` calls `SionController::indexAction()`, which fetches the entity's index
  through a path that throws `InvalidArgumentException: No entity provided.` when there
  are none — so five of the six libraries answer 500 here today, every one of them except
  Colegio Mayor, which holds all fourteen imports. An empty list is not an error, and the
  controller now renders one.

  The edit pencil appears only on a *pending* import: once an import has run, its file
  and columns are frozen, so linking to a form that cannot change them would be a link to
  a disabled page.

  The two download buttons are the entry point for a library that has never imported
  anything, which until 2026 was five of the six: the import matched one library's
  Spanish headings and the file had to already be on the server, so there was no way in.
  They sit beside "Start new import" because the file comes first.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}
{% import 'schoenstatt/_entity-format.html.twig' as format %}

{% block content %}
{% if is_allowed('route/library-imports/library/create') %}
<p>
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ laminas_path('library-imports/library/create', {'library_id': library_id}) }}">{{ translate('Start new import') }}</a>
  <a class="btn btn-default" href="{{ template_url }}">{{ translate('Blank template') }}</a>
  <a class="btn btn-default" href="{{ export_url }}">{{ translate('This library\'s books') }}</a>
</p>
<p class="help-block">{{ translate('Cataloguing in a spreadsheet is much faster than the web form. Download one of these, fill it in, and start an import with it.') }}</p>
{% endif %}
<table class="table">
<thead>
<tr>
    <th>{{ translate('Import name') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Description') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Status') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Complete import') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Import started') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Last updated') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Books created') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Books updated') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Books inactivated') }}</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{% for object in objects %}
<tr>
    <td>{{ format.entity('library-import', object, {'displayEditPencil': object.status == 'pending'}) }}</td>
    <td>{{ object.description }}</td>
    <td>{% if object.status == 'completed' %}{{ translate('Run') }}{% elseif object.status == 'abandoned' %}{{ translate('Abandoned') }}{% else %}{{ translate('Not run yet') }}{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ object.isCompleteImport ? translate('Yes') : translate('No') }}</td>
    <td>{{ medium_datetime(object.createdOn) }}</td>
    <td>{{ medium_datetime(object.updatedOn) }}</td>
    <td>{{ object.booksCreated }}</td>
    <td>{{ object.booksUpdated }}</td>
    <td>{{ object.booksInactivated }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endblock %}
